{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Both $49x^2$ and $9$ are *perfect squares,* since $49x^2=(\\blueD{7x})^2$ and $9=(\\greenD{3})^2$.\n\n$49x^2-9 = (\\blueD{7x})^2-(\\greenD{3})^2$\n\nSo we can use the *difference of squares* pattern to factor.\n\n$\\blueD{a}^2 - \\greenD{b}^2 =(\\blueD{a}+\\greenD{b})(\\blueD{a}-\\greenD{b})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In this case, $\\blueD{a}=\\blueD{7x}$ and $\\greenD{b}=\\greenD{3}$:\n\n$(\\blueD{7x})^2 - (\\greenD{3})^2 =(\\blueD{7x}+\\greenD{3})(\\blueD{7x}-\\greenD{3})$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$49x^2-9=(7x+3)(7x-3)$\n\n*Remember that you can always check your factorization by expanding it.*","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor completely.**\n\n$49x^2-9=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"(7x+3)(7x-3)"},{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":1,"simplify":false,"value":"-(3+7x)(3-7x)"}],"buttonSets":["basic"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
